## How it works

The table is the scorecard's own input: the same population (the stream's paths,
or every assigned path with `assignment`), the same window (events before
`assigned_at` dropped, `horizon` applied) and the same per-path values as
[`get_ab_test`](/docs/tools/get-ab-test). Silent paths are 0 for 0/1 metrics and
totals; a value metric is NaN where it is undefined (`time_between` without both
events), so its mean runs over the paths with a value, as the scorecard's does; a
ratio metric comes as numerator and denominator, and its arm value is the summed
numerator over the summed denominator. Paths that a `horizon` leaves out stay in
the table with `mature=False`, so the analysed population is
`paths[paths["mature"]]`.

The scorecard covers the standard tests. Anything else starts from this table:
variance reduction with a pre-period covariate (CUPED, regression adjustment),
quantile or rank tests, a custom plot of the per-path distribution, or the
variance of a metric from history to plan the next test's sample size.

